{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/youngi"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/youngI","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","title":"youngI","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE6youngIAEvpZ","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]},"modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"youngI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"roleHeading":"Type Property","extendedModule":"IvorTuning"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"youngI"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, and A→E — are each narrowed by 3\/16 of the syntonic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comma, equal to (3\/2)·(80\/81)^(3\/16) ≈ 697.923 cents. Four more fifths — E→B,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"B→F♯, B♭→F, and F→C — are each narrowed by (¼ PC − 3\/16 SC) ≈ 1.833 cents,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equal to (3\/2)·(81\/80)^(3\/16)·(2¹⁹\/3¹²)^(−1\/4) ≈ 700.122 cents. The remaining","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"four fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Published in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" 90 (1800).","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Young I (Thomas Young, 1800).","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","title":"IvorTuning","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/TuningSystem/youngI":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"youngI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/youngi","title":"youngI","role":"symbol","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Young I (Thomas Young, 1800)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/youngI"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths."}],"role":"symbol","title":"WellTemperament","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/TuningSystem":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem","title":"TuningSystem","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TuningSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TuningSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that describes a musical tuning system."}]}}}